 "24 – 28 September 1988"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/635"} "Ol-lim-pik Ju-gyeong-gi-jang, Seoul Sports Complex, Seoul"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/63309"} "75 from 55 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "In early August 1988, at the Weltklasse Meet in Zürich, " [:a {:href "/athletes/78943"} "Harry “Butch” Reynolds"] " broke Lee Evans’s vaunted world record of 43.86 from the 1968 Olympics, running 43.29. He was a heavy favorite in Seoul, and had also won the US Olympic Trials from " [:a {:href "/athletes/78381"} "Danny Joe Everett"] ". The third US qualifier was a youngster, Everett’s 19-year-old " [:a {:href "/affiliations/289"} "UCLA"] " teammate, " [:a {:href "/athletes/78693"} "Steve Lewis"] ". In the first two rounds at Seoul, Lewis had the fastest times. The two semis were won by Reynolds and Lewis, with 1987 World Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/70512"} "Thomas Schönlebe"] " (GDR) failing to qualify. In the final, Everett opened up early and led to 200 metres. Lewis then took the lead but Reynolds was closing. His last 100 was the fastest but he narrowly missed catching Lewis, who won the gold. Everett held on to complete the US sweep."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1103"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78693"} "Steve Lewis"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "45.31 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "44.41 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "44.35 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "43.87 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style "